Rolling a fair die is modelled by $Omega = {1, ..., 6}$, $cal(F) = cal(P)(Omega)$ and $PP(A) = abs(A)/6$ for every $A in cal(F)$.

Picking $k$ of $n$ labelled balls at random without replacement is modelled by $Omega = {A subset.eq {1, ..., n} : abs(A) = k}$, so $abs(Omega) = binom(n, k)$ and $PP({omega}) = 1 \/ binom(n, k)$ for each outcome $omega$.
